    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d780">

                <pb facs="0794" n="536" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg536"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2089</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-09-07T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 7, 1915, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2154. Your 2824, September 2.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d780-f1"/> On September 1 the
                    German Ambassador wrote me as follows:</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>I beg to inform you that my instructions concerning our answer to your last
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Lusitania</hi> note contain the following
                        passage: “Liners will not be sunk by our submarines without warning and
                        without safety of the lives of non-combatants, provided that the liners do
                        not try to escape or offer resistance.” Although I know that you do not wish
                        to discuss the <hi rendition="#italic">Lusitania</hi> question till the <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Arabic</hi> incident has been definitely and
                        satisfactorily settled, I desire to inform you of the above because this
                        policy of my Government was decided on before the <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Arabic</hi> incident occurred.</p>
                </quote>
                <p>As this note indicates that a further communication from the German Government
                    may be expected, please bring this matter to the attention of the Minister of
                    Foreign Affairs and request to be informed when this Government may expect a
                    full statement in regard to the <hi rendition="#italic">Arabic</hi> case.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
